	(text "BLE (Raytac MDBT42T-P, nRF52805) - ported from Yuhka hub 'Bluetooth LE' sheet (commit 33ea1da), reworked:\n- UART1 bridge to STM32: UART1_TX = STM PB6 -> BLE P0.16 (RX), UART1_RX = STM PB7 <- BLE P0.18 (TX).\n- BLE can drive STM BOOT0 (P0.12) and NRST (P0.14, open-drain!) -> STM firmware update over BLE.\n  Check AN2606: is USART1 on PB6/PB7 a bootloader UART on STM32C5? If not, do OTA via own STM bootloader.\n- BLE_IRQ (P0.05 -> STM PB5) as wake/attention line. Spare GPIOs to STM: P0.04 = BLE_GPIO1 (PB4),\n  P0.01/XL2 = BLE_GPIO2 (PA15).\n  - BLE_BTN (P0.00/XL1): bind/pairing button SW501 to GND, R501 10k pull-up (works before firmware configures pull-ups). BLE_LED (P0.20) drives an LED on the UX sheet.\n- LDO mode only (like the original Yuhka sheet): DCC not connected, DEC4 gets its 1uF. Never set NRF_POWER->DCDCEN.\n- No 32k crystal: use LFRC (P0.00/P0.01 are free as GPIO). PCB: keep copper out from under the antenna end."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
